if {game_state} == 3.0:
	if {crow_educated} == 0.0:
		Crow: You were lucky I was there kid
		Crow: Do you even understand how close you came to losing your soul and remaining their pet for eternity?
		You: Well no… They didn’t seem so bad…
		You: …just looking for new dance partners—
		Crow: You have a lot to learn, kid
		Crow: The fae never give for free and are quite liberal in what they decide is an equivalent exchange if ya don’t make one yourself
		You: Oh wow… I had no idea
		You: Thank you so much for your help Mr. Crow!
		Crow: Don’t thank me yet kid
		Crow: You’re lucky I am not of the Fair Folk, or your soul would be mine now ~keh keh kehh~
		Crow: ’ll tell you what\: I’m gathering materials for my nest
		Crow: If you can find me what I need, I’ll give ya the berries in exchange
		Crow: I WAS the one to make  the deal after all , you’re welcome
		You: Alright… I guess I would have been lost—worse than lost—without you
		You: Mr. Crow. I owe you a favor. We have a deal!
		Crow: Perfect, perfect! Yer an agreeable one, aren’t ya kid?
		Crow: I have a good feeling about you and your capabilities in gathering all the materials necessary for me
		Crow: I need something soft,\
		something shiny,\
		something twiggy,\
		and something sticky.
		Crow: Come back to  me when you’ve gathered them all, and you’ll have yer berries
		Crow: That’s a promise!
		set {crow_educated} = 1.0
	elif {crow_educated} == 1.0:
		if {all_things_gathered} == 0.0:
			if {ListsForDialogic.crow_size} == 1.0:
				Faunus: You’ve done well so far kid, but you’re still missing something... Right! You still gotta find me {ListsForDialogic.crow_missing[0]}, Come back when you’ve finished!
			elif {ListsForDialogic.crow_size} == 2.0:
				Faunus: You’ve done well so far kid, but you’re still missing something... Right! You still gotta find me {ListsForDialogic.crow_missing[0]} and {ListsForDialogic.crow_missing[1]}, Come back when you’ve finished!
			elif {ListsForDialogic.crow_size} == 3.0:
				Faunus: You’ve done well so far kid, but you’re still missing something... Right! You still gotta find me {ListsForDialogic.crow_missing[0]}, {ListsForDialogic.crow_missing[1]} and {ListsForDialogic.crow_missing[2]}, Come back when you’ve finished!
			elif {ListsForDialogic.crow_size} == 4.0:
				Crow: I need something soft,\
				something shiny,\
				something twiggy,\
				and something sticky.
				Crow: Come back to me when you’ve gathered them all, and you’ll have yer berries
				Crow: That’s a promise!
		else:
			Crow: Good going! I’m impressed kid
			Crow: you almost have an eye as sharp as a crow’s ~keh keh keh~
			Crow: Of course, yours could never be quite so keen as to see all that us corvids can
			Crow: but for a mortal, you contain more of the spirit of the crow than even most kinds of the Fair Folk…
			Crow: In fact, for a mortal, I can see the spirits of so many creatures and flora of this forest swirling through you
			Crow: If I didn’t know any better than to recognize the distinctive mortal stench wafting off of you
			Crow: I’d have half a mind to question if you’re even mortal at all
			Crow: Or what you even are
			Crow: The only other being I’ve ever seen who contains such a swirl of various forest spirits within...
			Crow: Well, I’d best end that thought there
			Crow: Still, no use poking my beak where it doesn’t concern me
			You: Hold on a second!
			You: Maybe not you Mr. Crow, but it very much concerns me!
			You: What’s wrong with me?
			You: I’m mortal?
			You: I’m technically not mortal?
			You: I have all these spirits in my body and no one can see them but you a-a-an—?
			Crow: Sorry, can’t tell ya who the other fella I know is who has all of these flora and fauna swirling around inside of themself similarly to you
			Crow: Although he’s far more embodied than you are
			Crow: Then again, I wouldn’t think to blame a sapling for not yet having the strength of an ancient oak
			Crow: Well alrighty then, before I truly say too much
			Crow: time for me to fulfill my end of the bargain
			Crow: Here’s your berries, as promised!
			Crow: Best of luck getting through your duties without getting caught up in any more fae mischief, kid
			Crow: I’m not always gonna be around to save your backside if you get sloppy in your engagements and negotiations ~keh keh keh~
			set {game_state} = 4.0
			[signal arg="give berries"]
elif {game_state} >= 4.0 and {game_state} < 6.0:
	Crow: we're even now
elif {game_state} == 6.0:
	Crow: Hey there kid. Hope those berries were tasty
	Crow: Do you think they woulda been worth the cost of yer soul? ~keh keh~
	You: They weren’t exactly for me
	You: but I think the bear found them quite tasty
	You: Thank you again for your help Mr. Crow
	You: Did you happen to see a carving knife around?
	You: Faunus thought he left it by the shack, but he can’t find it
	You: It’s pretty important!
	Crow: Maybe I have
	Crow: Maybe I haven’t
	Crow: What’s it to you that the old goat wants it?
	You: I need to play a melody to awaken the first flower of spring, and well…
	You: I don’t exactly have an instrument
	You: Faunus said he would make me a fiddle
	You: but he needs his knife for that
	You: I know how much you love shiny things
	You: so I thought you would be the best bird to ask about finding it
	Crow: I may have found a shiny knife lying around
	Crow: Nobody was claiming it
	Crow: You know how it is, kid
	Crow: finders keepers
	You: It’s really important to him though
	You: And it’s really important to the entire forest that he carve me a fiddle
	You: or spring will never come to the forest
	Crow: That surely matters for your sake too, doesn’t it?
	Crow: Alright, calm down kid
	Crow: Tell you what
	Crow: I’ll let you borrow MY knife for this purpose
	Crow: as long as you bring it back to me once you’re done
	Crow: of course alongside an invitation to this performance I am so generously sponsoring
	You: I can do that!
	You: Thank you so much, Mr. Crow!
	You: Of course you can watch the performance
	You: I don’t know how good I’ll really be however
	You: I’m not much of a musician
	Crow: Maybe not, but you’ve been full of surprises
	Crow: Even yer presence is something I haven’t felt in this forest in a long while
	Crow: I think you really might be what that old goat has been looking for all these years
	You: What are you saying?
	Crow: Well really, that’s between you an’ him
	Crow: I just want to watch how it all plays out from a crow’s eye view
	Crow: I’ll give ya this kid
	Crow: yer interesting enough to make parting with something so lovingly polished and shined not too bad of a deal
	Crow: Here ya go
	Crow: Let me know when it’s showtime
	Crow: I bet it’ll be a performance for the ages, nerves and all ~keh keh keh~
	[signal arg="give knife"]
elif {game_state} >= 7.0 and {game_state} < 8.0:
	if {crow_invited} == 0.0:
		Crow: So it’s finally show time, kid?
		You: It is. Faunus is just finishing building the fiddle for me to play while I collect you for the performance
		Crow: Glad to hear yer nerves aren’t getting the best of ya at least ~keh keh~
		Crow: I’ll see you soon, kid
		Crow: I can’t wait to see how this finally goes down
		set {crow_invited} = 1.0
	elif {crow_invited} == 1.0:
		Crow: I can’t wait to see how this finally goes down
elif {game_state} == 8.0:
	Crow: Splendid performance kid
	Crow: Almost enough to make us even
	Crow: Almost